    "body": "Six defects found while running the PC/SC examples of `keyple-cpp-example` against a SpringCard Puck SAM and an Identive CLOUD 2700 R holding a Calypso SAM C1.\n\nAll six are divergences from the Java reference implementation, not Windows workarounds. The first one only becomes visible under the MSVC debug heap, which fills uninitialised memory with a recognisable pattern instead of zeros.\n\nOne commit per defect, each message stating the observed symptom.\n\n### Commits\n\n- `e9f2955` **default-initialise the digest manager state flags.** Three bools had no initialiser and came up true, so the SAM received a Digest Close with no Digest Init and answered 6985.\n- `3e95d45` **throw command exceptions instead of returning them by value.** `buildCommandException` returned a `CommandException` by value, slicing every derived exception to the base class, which made each `catch` on a derived type unreachable. Renamed `throwCommandException`, declared `[[noreturn]] void`.\n- `38b8cf9` **declare the real response length of the digest update commands.** Both declared a fixed 8-byte response. Digest Update only returns data in encrypted session mode and Digest Update Multiple never does, so the length check rejected a successful 9000.\n- `e0f9686` **declare no response data for Give Random.** The expected length was the size of the random value transmitted, while the SAM answers with a status word only. The length check turned a successful 9000 into the misleading error \"Give Random [9000]\".\n- `998dc71` **use the verification constructor when ciphering a PIN to present.** `cipherPin` always called the PIN modification constructor, which sets P1 to 40h and rejects an empty new PIN, making encrypted PIN verification impossible. The verification constructor, setting P1 to 80h, was dead code.\n- `a2dbf27` **send P2=A8h for PSO Verify Signature.** P2 was ABh, two digits transposed, and the SAM rejected the command with 6B00, wrong P1 or P2, so the verification logic was never reached. The resulting APDU now matches the Java reference byte for byte.\n\n### Validation\n\nEach fix was validated on hardware through the example that exposed it. `UseCase6_VerifyPin` and `UseCase9_ChangePin` exercise the ciphered PIN paths, `UseCase11_DataSigning` the PSO Verify Signature path, and `UseCase4_CardAuthentication` and `UseCase12_PerformanceMeasurement` the digest path. APDU traces were compared against the output of the Java examples on the same SAM.\n",
